xt-right">388,120</td><td data-slot="table-cell" class="p-2 align-middle whitespace-nowrap [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0 [&amp;&gt;[role=checkbox]]:translate-y-[2px] hidden sm:table-cell text-right"><span>0</span></td></tr><tr><td data-slot="table-cell" class="p-2 whitespace-nowrap [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0 [&amp;&gt;[role=checkbox]]:translate-y-[2px] font-medium align-top"><div class="flex items-end gap-1">12<span class="text-xs text-negative">↓1</span></div></td><td data-slot="table-cell" class="p-2 align-middle [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0 [&amp;&gt;[role=checkbox]]:translate-y-[2px] whitespace-normal"><div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1"><a class="flex items-center gap-2" href="/package/npm/tidepool"><span class="flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-muted text-muted-foreground"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-4" aria-hidden="true" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M1.763 0C.786 0 0 .786 0 1.763v20.474C0 23.214.786 24 1.763 24h20.474c.977 0 1.763-.786 1.763-1.763V1.763C24 .786 23.214 0 22.237 0zM5.13 5.323l13.837.019-.009 13.836h-3.464l.01-10.382h-3.456L12.04 19.17H5.113z"></path></svg></span><span translate="no" class="min-w-0 [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">tidepool</span></a></div></td><td data-slot="table-cell" class="p-2 align-middle whitespace-nowrap [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0 [&amp;&gt;[role=checkbox]]:translate-y-[2px] hidden md:table-cell"></td><td data-slot="table-cell" class="p-2 align-middle whitespace-nowrap [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0 [&amp;&gt;[role=checkbox]]:translate-y-[2px] text-right">96,210</td><td data-slot="table-cell" class="p-2 align-middle whitespace-nowrap [&amp;:has([role=checkbox])]:pr-0 [&amp;&gt;[role=checkbox]]:translate-y-[2px] hidden sm:table-cell text-right"><span class="text-negative">−1,155</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground" data-testid="ranking-stats">At the latest monthly read, 41,870 npm packages are used directly by at least one repository with 100+ stars. By weekly downloads, the top three are <a class="transition-colors duration-200 underline text-inherit hover:text-foreground" href="/package/npm/moss-date">moss-date</a> (5,806,310), <a class="transition-colors duration-200 underline text-inherit hover:text-foreground" href="/package/npm/@orbit/fetch">@orbit/fetch</a> (3,120,664) and <a class="transition-colors duration-200 underline text-inherit hover:text-foreground" href="/package/npm/kite-router">kite-router</a> (2,410,552). Only npm, only direct dependents, downloads to November 15, 2026. Ranks as of November 17, 2026. <a class="transition-colors duration-200 underline text-inherit hover:text-foreground" href="/methodology/packages">How package rankings work</a>.</p><section class="flex flex-col gap-4"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Questions</h2><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What does the npm package ranking by downloads count?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Rank is based on npm downloads in the 7 days to November 15, 2026. A package is ranked once at least one repository with 100+ stars uses it directly."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which npm package is first by weekly downloads?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"moss-date, with 5,806,310 downloads in the 7 days to November 15, 2026. Then @orbit/fetch and kite-router."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What counts as a dependent?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A public repository with 100+ stars that lists the package in its own package.json. Lockfiles, forks and example, docs or test folders don't count, and neither does a package that only comes in through another package."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How often are package rankings updated?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Dependents are read once a month, last on November 16, 2026. Ranks are worked out again after each monthly read and at least once a week; these are of November 17, 2026."}}]}</script><dl class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-sm"><div class="flex flex-col gap-1"><dt class="font-semibold">What does the npm package ranking by downloads count?</dt><dd class="text-muted-foreground">Rank is based on npm downloads in the 7 days to November 15, 2026. A package is ranked once at least one repository with 100+ stars uses it directly.</dd></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-1"><dt class="font-semibold">Which npm package is first by weekly downloads?</dt><dd class="text-muted-foreground">moss-date, with 5,806,310 downloads in the 7 days to November 15, 2026. Then @orbit/fetch and kite-router.</dd></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-1"><dt class="font-semibold">What counts as a dependent?</dt><dd class="text-muted-foreground">A public repository with 100+ stars that lists the package in its own package.json. Lockfiles, forks and example, docs or test folders don&#x27;t count, and neither does a package that only comes in through another package.</dd></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-1"><dt class="font-semibold">How often are package rankings updated?</dt><dd class="text-muted-foreground">Dependents are read once a month, last on November 16, 2026. Ranks are worked out again after each monthly read and at least once a week; these are of November 17, 2026.</dd></div></dl></section>"`;
